    <h3>Frequently Asked Questions About PDF Unlocking</h3>
    <div style="margin-top: 24px;">
      <div class="faq-accordion-item">
        <h4 class="faq-accordion-q">1. What should I do if I forgot the password to my bank statement PDF?</h4>
        <p class="faq-accordion-a">
          If you forgot the password to an encrypted bank statement, you cannot brute-force or bypass it directly because it uses cryptographic AES encryption. However, virtually all Indian banks use predictable formulaic passwords based on your personal information—such as your Date of Birth (in DDMMYYYY format), your Customer ID, PAN number, or the last 4 digits of your account or registered mobile number. Check our bank password formula table above to determine the exact pattern used by your bank (e.g., HDFC uses Customer ID; SBI uses DOB + @ + mobile digits; ICICI uses first 4 letters of name + DDMM).
        </p>
